<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<RunSettings>

  <RunConfiguration>
    <EnvironmentVariables>

      <!--
        Workaround for a defect of the .NET 10 runtime, tracked as https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/131267.
        The test host of this project crashed intermittently with "Fatal error. Internal CLR error. (0x80131506)"
        after every test had passed, which aborted the run and failed the public build.

        When the garbage collector suspends a thread that runs in code which is not fully interruptible, it hijacks
        the return address of the current method. The hijacked return value is reported to the collector through the
        garbage collection information of the calling method. CallDescrWorkerInternal, which the runtime uses for
        reflection invocation, is written in assembly and carries no such information, so an object reference left
        in the return register is neither reported nor updated. The heap is corrupted, and the process fails later
        at an unrelated read. xunit invokes every test method by reflection, so every test method is exposed.

        DOTNET_JitDebuggable makes the just-in-time compiler emit fully interruptible code for every method. The
        garbage collector then suspends threads in place instead of hijacking a return address, and the defect
        cannot occur. The cost is that this test host runs without optimizations.

        Remove this file, and the RunSettingsFilePath property that references it, once the build container
        installs a .NET 10 runtime of version 10.0.12 or later, which carries the fix. See
        https://github.com/metalama/Metalama/issues/1976.
      -->
      <DOTNET_JitDebuggable>1</DOTNET_JitDebuggable>

    </EnvironmentVariables>
  </RunConfiguration>

</RunSettings>
